  "slug": "quantum-rydberg-6779",
  "summary": "New preprints propose mediator-based and transversal gates, measurement-free error correction, and improved readout across ion, cavity, atom and spin platforms.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is control and error-management design for multi-qubit operations across platforms, with all items being preprints. One proposes reset-assisted control in which noisy mediator qubits drive high-fidelity gates on long-lived data qubits, analyzed with quantum trajectories. Another proposes parallel transversal controlled-Z gates across neighboring wells in a double-well trapped-ion architecture, with dynamical decoupling and crosstalk treatment. A measurement-free protocol for superconducting cavities corrects single-photon loss without syndrome readout. Supporting items address confidence-aware readout of 171Yb tweezer arrays, which matches fidelity with half the imaging time, a phonon-aware Lindblad model of electron-to-nuclear spin transfer in NV centers, and a review of qudit control across several platforms. Most results are proposals or simulations rather than experimental demonstrations.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
